Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds two related changes:

1. cdd/post-release/SKILL.md §4 (Review Quality)
   - new per-cycle round-counts table (cycle / issue / mode / rounds /
     binding findings R1 / notes)
   - finding-class breakdown expanded to 5 classes:
     mechanical / wiring / honest-claim / judgment / contract
   - new honest-claim ratio metric with target <30%

2. cdd/post-release/SKILL.md Step 2 + cdd/release/SKILL.md §2.4
   - CHANGELOG ledger row gains a Rounds column
   - format: | X.Y.Z | C_Σ | α | β | γ | Level | Rounds | Note |

Motivation: the cnos-tsc supercycle produced a 1 → 2 → 3 → 1 → 2
review-round trace across cycles 27, 25, 24, 26, 29. The arc
correlates with cycle complexity but more importantly with
accumulated context — once a team has run through one substantial
cycle, follow-on cycles run cleaner. Surfacing this in the ledger
makes it visible across releases instead of being buried in
per-cycle PRA prose.

Adding 'wiring' and 'honest-claim' as first-class finding classes
reflects the supercycle evidence that beta's most valuable findings
were in these categories (e.g. extract_deltas not wired into
main.ml, gauge_witness not called from report.ml, false claim in
SELF-MEASURE.md about engine derivation, score discrepancy in the
self-coherence report). The mechanical/judgment binary was too
coarse.
